			"description": "<ul><li>Users can configure HTTP monitors to perform deep health checks on JSON API endpoints, going beyond a simple HTTP 200 OK status</li><li>This is achieved by specifying a JMESPath query to target a specific key in the JSON response</li><li>An expected value and a match method (e</li><li>g</li><li>, 'equal', 'include', 'regex') can be set to validate the API's data integrity, ensuring the service is not just online but also functioning correctly</li></ul>",
